44
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:31,940
Language Takeaway.

45
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:38,480
The first phrase we have today is one that's very important when you're looking for a job.

46
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:41,420
It's called job listing or job listings here.

47
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:42,780
Okay, job listings.

48
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:47,000
And this is really common before the internet existed.

49
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:50,040
You would have the listings in your local newspaper, right?

50
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:50,520
Exactly.

51
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:56,100
In the movies, you always had the person sitting with the newspaper circling the potential jobs.

52
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:58,320
Right, with a red marker.

53
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,320
Exactly.

54
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:02,400
But now that we have the internet, you have lots of websites that have job listings.

55
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:07,080
And so a job listing is literally a list of jobs that are available.

56
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:07,260
Okay.

57
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,140
So you look through the job listings.

58
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,600
Maybe you found one that's interesting.

59
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:11,920
There's an email address.

60
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,100
So what do they ask for?

61
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:15,800
They ask you to send in your resume.

62
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:16,960
Okay.

63
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:19,880
A resume is very important when you're looking for a job.

64
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,160
It's a document.

65
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:31,860
It's a piece of paper that tells someone all of the work that you've done before, your job experiences, and it tells them where you went to school and what your qualifications are.

66
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,580
So it's a summary of your work life.

67
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:35,160
Okay.

68
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:36,980
And that's why it's called a resume, right?

69
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:40,340
It's pretty much a summary of your work life, as you say.

70
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,360
That's right.

71
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:48,590
And a different one, sometimes people use this, is a CV, curriculum vitae, and that's an academic summary of your life.

72
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:51,830
So you have the work summary and the study summary.

73
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:52,570
Okay.

74
00:03:52,810 --> 00:03:53,290
Very good.

75
00:03:53,950 --> 00:03:58,510
So if you send in your resume, what's recommended is that you attach it with a cover letter.

76
00:03:59,240 --> 00:03:59,780
Okay.

77
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:01,720
Well, cover letter, you know the word letter.

78
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:04,000
It's something that you write to somebody else.

79
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:07,020
But a cover letter is like a cover for your resume.

80
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:16,760
It's a letter where you explain to the future boss or future employer what exactly you want and how this job is going to help you get it.

81
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:17,440
Okay.

82
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:21,520
So that's basically a small little introduction to yourself, right?

83
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:26,440
Before they read your resume, who you are, what you're looking for, maybe very quickly.

84
00:04:26,510 --> 00:04:26,830
Exactly.

85
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,120
So you can say, Hi, my name is Catherine.

86
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:37,090
I'm very motivated and excited to have the opportunity to talk to you about why I'm a skilled employee and why I will benefit your company.

87
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:37,930
Very good.

88
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:39,720
All right.

89
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,070
So you've sent in your resume and your cover letter.

90
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:45,710
And well, maybe you're looking to get into a career as a gas station attendant.

91
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:49,710
So what's the difference between job and career?

92
00:04:50,070 --> 00:04:50,290
Okay.

93
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:59,120
And this is very interesting because in many languages, there is a similar word, which for example, in Spanish is carrera, right?

94
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:01,010
And that means like a profession.

95
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:05,690
So many people translate it literally as career, but it's not the right word.

96
00:05:05,870 --> 00:05:06,590
What is a career?

97
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:11,750
A career I think of as a long term goal.

98
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,820
A career is your profession.

99
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:15,930
It's the name you give yourself.

100
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:21,000
But a job is a position in a company from one time to another.

101
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:25,320
So for example, my job here is host of EnglishPod.

102
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,620
But maybe in the future, I will have a media career.

103
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:34,040
That means that my job or jobs will have to do with this profession.

104
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,640
It's kind of a bigger thing, a longer thing.

105
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,260
So maybe you can think of it this way.

106
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:43,920
A career is like, as you say, bigger picture, like the macro category, right?

107
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:46,180
You're into media and television, for example.

108
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,750
And your job specifically is a podcast host.

109
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:58,030
But in the future, maybe I want to have a different job in this career and move into production and be a TV producer.

110
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:01,080
So that's a part of my career path.

111
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:03,120
I can move forward.

112
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:05,000
So career is very important word.

113
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:05,210
All right.

