134
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:33,500
It's going to make you sound very fluent in English if you use it.

135
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,560
We say in the market for.

136
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:38,000
I'm in the market for a new job.

137
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:38,920
All right.

138
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:41,680
So this person is looking for a new job.

139
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,880
He is in the market for.

140
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:47,660
I could also say, I'm in the market for a new house.

141
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:50,180
Marco, do you know any good real estate agents?

142
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:56,200
So what does that mean if you say I'm in the market for a new job or you're in the market for a new house?

143
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:59,840
I am right now actively looking for this thing.

144
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:00,920
I really want one.

145
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:01,700
You're available.

146
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,320
Yes.

147
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:04,320
Okay.

148
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:08,000
So I'm in the market for a new job.

149
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:09,880
I'm in the market for a new car.

150
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,520
It means the market is the marketplace.

151
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:13,380
Right, right.

152
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:16,790
And this sometimes you could see it related in movies.

153
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:21,330
For example, they say if a person gets married, they are no longer in the market.

154
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:23,470
I'm in the market for a husband.

155
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,680
Right.

156
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:25,050
Do you know any nice guys?

157
00:08:25,710 --> 00:08:26,410
All right.

158
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,230
So you're in the market.

159
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:29,130
You're looking for a job.

160
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:33,710
And well, if you're qualified, it will be a piece of cake to find a new job.

161
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:35,730
Isn't this a delicious phrase?

162
00:08:36,450 --> 00:08:39,190
So piece of cake, you think what does cake have to do with anything?

163
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,760
Well, cake, this is a way to say something is easy.

164
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,040
Okay, so it's really easy.

165
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:51,900
This often happens in our office actually, because you and I understand computers, but we work with someone who has a hard time with computers.

166
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:54,480
And she's like, oh, it doesn't work.

167
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:55,720
And we're like, it's a piece of cake.

168
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,120
It's a piece of cake.

169
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:57,640
It's so easy.

170
00:08:58,260 --> 00:08:59,040
Why is this hard?

171
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:02,200
So a piece of cake is a way to say something simple.

172
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:05,180
And it's a very, very, very common phrase.

173
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,400
You'll hear it all the time.

174
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:08,360
A piece of cake, don't worry about it.

175
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:08,760
Piece of cake.

176
00:09:09,170 --> 00:09:10,490
Hey, can you help me out with this thing?

177
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:11,610
Sure, it's a piece of cake.

178
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:12,910
All right.

179
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:16,870
And for our last phrase, he was talking about his position as a gas attendant.

180
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:23,750
And he said, well, you know, all the greats, all the famous people, they started somewhere before they made it big.

181
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:26,350
What does he mean with they made it big?

182
00:09:26,910 --> 00:09:32,670
Well, the phrase to make it big or in here in the past tense, made it big, means to be successful.

183
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:36,660
So we're talking about, for example, Albert Einstein.

184
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:41,720
Albert Einstein worked in the patent office in a clue.

185
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:43,580
He was a clerk in Europe.

186
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,360
And you know, that's not a very impressive job, but it was a job.

187
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:52,800
And he made it big later on as a physicist.

188
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:58,000
And so to make it big is to succeed, to become famous or successful or important.

189
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Right.

190
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,120
Or sometimes people say, yeah, I made it.

191
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:02,260
I made it big or I made it in my life.

192
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:03,760
And that means that you were successful.

193
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,080
Or this product is going to make it big.

194
00:10:06,660 --> 00:10:07,860
It's going to be really successful.

195
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:09,080
Yeah, that's good.

196
00:10:09,220 --> 00:10:09,520
Okay.

197
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:12,780
So it's a key phrase to make it or to make it big.

